      <dico>Lessing</dico>
      <unicode>ᠣᠷᠺᠢᠭᠣᠯᠢ</unicode>
      <uighur>orkiγuli</uighur>
      <cyrillic>орхиуль</cyrillic>
      <transcript>ORKIΓULI</transcript>
      <definition>[= orkiγul] n. The two ends of a ceremonial rosary extending beyond the large ornamental bead, usually hanging down the back of the neck; long tuft of strings of red silk attached to the back of the ceremonial hat of women , and coming down to the waist and even lower.</definition>
      <page>619</page>
